node_modules/
dist/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/

# Game-derived data: generated locally from your own master.mdb, never committed.
packages/data/generated/*.json
!packages/data/generated/.gitkeep

# Never commit the game database itself.
*.mdb

# Local scratch: one-off diagnostics, probes, and delivered patches.
# They are how this project works, and none of them belong in history.
#
#   tools/diagnose/   TypeScript, run against the engine:  npx tsx tools/diagnose/<name>.ts
#   tools/probe/      Python, read master.mdb read-only:   python tools/probe/<name>.py
#
# Both directories are ignored wholesale, so neither exists in a fresh clone --
# create them as needed. The name globs stay as a backstop for anything that
# lands in the repo root by habit.
tools/diagnose/
tools/probe/
diagnose-*.ts
probe-*.py
*.patch

# tools/vision/ is NOT in that list, deliberately.
#
# The rule above is about scratch: a diagnostic answers a question and dies, and
# none of them belong in history. tools/vision/ is the opposite -- induce.ts
# GENERATES a committed artefact, packages/engine/src/vision/glyphs.ts, and
# corpus.ts defines the held-out split the accuracy figures in
# docs/m3c-vision.md are measured on. Ignored, the templates become
# unreproducible: nobody could rebuild them after a layout change or a new
# capture, and nobody could check the split the numbers rest on.
#
# What IS ignored is the intermediate it writes on the way, since the .ts file
# is the real output and two copies drift.
tools/vision/glyphs.json
tools/vision/out/
